{"name":"Aloe Vera Tea","hex":"#848b71","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aloe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The resins of the tree Aquilaria malaccensis (syn. Aquilaria agallocha), known for their fragrant aroma, produced after infection by the fungus Phialophora parasitica.","Any plant of the large and variable genus Aloe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloe"},{"term":"vera","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A skin (rolling paper for cigarettes)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A second-order measure of derivative price sensitivity, expressed as the rate of change of vega with respect to changes in the risk-free interest rate, or equivalently the rate of change of rho with respect to changes in the volatility of the underlying asset."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vera"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aloe vera","blocks":[{"text":"Aloe vera is a succulent plant species of the genus Aloe. It is widely distributed and is considered an invasive species in many regions of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Aloe_vera_flower_inset.png/330px-Aloe_vera_flower_inset.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe_vera","wikidata":"Q80079"},{"title":"Aloe","blocks":[{"text":"Aloe is a genus containing 594 species of flowering succulent plants. The most widely known species is Aloe vera, or \"true aloe\", which is cultivated as a source for topical uses and dietary supplements. Other species, such as Aloe ferox, are also cultivated or harvested from the wild for similar applications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Aloe_arborescens_on_Monte_Vumba_%284387600468%29.jpg/330px-Aloe_arborescens_on_Monte_Vumba_%284387600468%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe","wikidata":"Q127134"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg/500px-Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg/1280px-Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg/500px-Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Teeth on the leaf edge","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aloe_Vera.jpg/500px-Aloe_Vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aloe_Vera.jpg/1280px-Aloe_Vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont